                  "obligationId": "scenario%3Afile-owner-without-destination-write-grant::entry%3Apost-process-file",
                  "decision": {
                    "kind": "observed",
                    "observed": "allow"
                  },
                  "branchResults": [],
                  "explanation": "Within the supplied declared-entry source, the verified-user dependency is applied at process_file, and a non-admin file lookup is constrained by the caller's user ID. That is source-file ownership/association validation, not authorization to write to the caller-selected destination collection. When collection_name is supplied, process_file preserves that value and invokes save_docs_to_vector_db with add=True. save_docs_to_vector_db reaches VECTOR_DB_CLIENT.insert for that collection. The supplied process_file path does not call _validate_collection_access or otherwise check destination ownership or an explicit destination write grant before the insert. Therefore, under the fixed premises and accepted policy, the source-visible behavior is that the write is reachable: a verified non-admin who owns the file can cause its content to be inserted into the existing selected collection despite lacking destination write permission. The separately shown collection-access validator is not connected to this traced path in the supplied source.",
                  "facts": [
                    {
                      "id": "f-entry",
                      "kind": "entry",
                      "statement": "POST /process/file is implemented by process_file and obtains the caller through get_verified_user.",
